msgid "Set a device's memalloc_noio flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:207
#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:106
msgid "``bool enable``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:206
msgid "True for setting the flag and False for clearing the flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:207
msgid ""
"Set the flag for all devices in the path from the device to the root device "
"in the device tree if **enable** is true, otherwise clear the flag for "
"devices in the path whose siblings don't set the flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:211
msgid ""
"The function should only be called by block device, or network device driver "
"for solving the deadlock problem during runtime resume/suspend:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:215
msgid ""
"If memory allocation with GFP_KERNEL is called inside runtime resume/suspend "
"callback of any one of its ancestors(or the block device itself), the "
"deadlock may be triggered inside the memory allocation since it might not "
"complete until the block device becomes active and the involved page I/O "
"finishes. The situation is pointed out first by Alan Stern. Network device "
"are involved in iSCSI kind of situation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:223
msgid ""
"The lock of dev_hotplug_mutex is held in the function for handling hotplug "
"race because pm_runtime_set_memalloc_noio() may be called in async probe()."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:227
msgid ""
"The function should be called between device_add() and device_del() on the "
"affected device(block/network device)."
msgstr ""

