msgid "Target device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1259
msgid ""
"Increment the runtime PM usage counter of **dev** if its runtime PM status "
"is already ``RPM_ACTIVE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1263
#: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1283
msgid ""
"``-EINVAL``: Runtime PM is disabled for **dev**. The usage counter is not "
"incremented."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1264
#: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1284
msgid "``1``: Success; usage counter is incremented."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1265
msgid "``0``: **dev** was not active."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1277
msgid ""
"Increment the runtime PM usage counter of **dev** if it is \"in use.\" A "
"device is considered in use if its runtime PM status is ``RPM_ACTIVE`` and "
"its runtime PM usage counter is greater than 0, or if it is not ignoring "
"children and its active child count is nonzero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1285
msgid "``0``: **dev** was not in use; usage counter is not incremented."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1295
msgid "Set runtime PM status of a device and clear errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1298
msgid "``unsigned int status``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1297
msgid "New runtime PM status of the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1298
msgid ""
"If runtime PM of the device is disabled or its power.runtime_error field is "
"different from zero, the status may be changed either to RPM_ACTIVE, or to "
"RPM_SUSPENDED, as long as that reflects the actual state of the device. "
"However, if the device has a parent and the parent is not active, and the "
"parent's power.ignore_children flag is unset, the device's status cannot be "
"set to RPM_ACTIVE, so -EBUSY is returned in that case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1305
msgid ""
"If successful, __pm_runtime_set_status() clears the power.runtime_error "
"field and the device parent's counter of unsuspended children is modified to "
"reflect the new status.  If the new status is RPM_SUSPENDED, an idle "
"notification request for the parent is submitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1310
msgid ""
"If **dev** has any suppliers (as reflected by device links to them), and "
"**status** is RPM_ACTIVE, they will be activated upfront and if the "
"activation of one of them fails, the status of **dev** will be changed to "
"RPM_SUSPENDED (instead of the **status** value) and the suppliers will be "
"deactivated on exit.  The error returned by the failing supplier activation "
"will be returned in that case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1467
msgid "Flush pending requests and wait for completions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1469
msgid ""
"If the device has a pending resume request, resume it synchronously. For all "
"other request types, cancel any queued request, and wait for running "
"operations to complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1473
msgid ""
"Note that this is intentionally asymmetric, as it guarantees any queued "
"asynchronous resume request will complete, but it may cancel asynchronous "
"suspend requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1560
msgid "Enable runtime PM for a device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1562
msgid ""
"Enable runtime PM transitions for **dev** by decrementing its disable "
"counter. Once the counter reaches zero, the PM core is permitted to execute "
"runtime PM callbacks for **dev** as power conditions change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1566
msgid ""
"Callers should ensure that the device's runtime PM status accurately "
"reflects its physical hardware state (via pm_runtime_set_active() or "
"pm_runtime_set_suspended()) before enabling runtime PM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1608
msgid "set_active version of devm_pm_runtime_enable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1634
msgid "devres-enabled version of pm_runtime_enable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1637
#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:857
msgid "**NOTE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1637
msgid ""
"this will also handle calling pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend() for you at "
"driver exit time if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1654
msgid "devres-enabled version of pm_runtime_get_noresume."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1666
msgid "Block runtime PM of a device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1668
msgid ""
"Resume **dev** if already suspended and block runtime suspend of **dev** in "
"such a way that it can be unblocked via the /sys/devices/.../power/control "
"interface, or otherwise by calling pm_runtime_allow()."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1672
#: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1699
msgid ""
"Calling this function many times in a row has the same effect as calling it "
"once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1692
msgid "Unblock runtime PM of a device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1694
msgid ""
"Unblock runtime suspend of **dev** after it has been blocked by "
"pm_runtime_forbid() (for instance, if it has been blocked via the /sys/"
"devices/.../power/control interface), check if **dev** can be suspended and "
"suspend it in that case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1724
msgid "Ignore runtime PM callbacks for a device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1726
msgid ""
"Set the power.no_callbacks flag, which tells the PM core that this device is "
"power-managed through its parent and has no runtime PM callbacks of its "
"own.  The runtime sysfs attributes will be removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1742
msgid "Leave interrupts disabled during callbacks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1743
msgid "Device to handle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1744
msgid ""
"Set the power.irq_safe flag, which tells the PM core that the "
"->runtime_suspend() and ->runtime_resume() callbacks for this device should "
"always be invoked with the spinlock held and interrupts disabled.  It also "
"causes the parent's usage counter to be permanently incremented, preventing "
"the parent from runtime suspending -- otherwise an irq-safe child might have "
"to wait for a non-irq-safe parent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1803
msgid "Set a device's autosuspend_delay value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1806
msgid "``int delay``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1805
msgid "Value of the new delay in milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1806
msgid ""
"Set the device's power.autosuspend_delay value.  If it changes to negative "
"and the power.use_autosuspend flag is set, prevent runtime suspends.  If it "
"changes the other way, allow runtime suspends."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1825
msgid "Set a device's use_autosuspend flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1828
msgid "``bool use``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1827
msgid "New value for use_autosuspend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:1828
msgid ""
"Set the device's power.use_autosuspend flag, and allow or prevent runtime "
"suspends as needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:2009
msgid "Force a device into suspend state if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:2011
msgid ""
"Disable runtime PM so we safely can check the device's runtime PM status and "
"if it is active, invoke its ->runtime_suspend callback to suspend it and "
"change its runtime PM status field to RPM_SUSPENDED.  Also, if the device's "
"usage and children counters don't indicate that the device was in use before "
"the system-wide transition under way, decrement its parent's children "
"counter (if there is a parent).  Keep runtime PM disabled to preserve the "
"state unless we encounter errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:2019
msgid ""
"Typically this function may be invoked from a system suspend callback to "
"make sure the device is put into low power state and it should only be used "
"during system-wide PM transitions to sleep states.  It assumes that the "
"analogous pm_runtime_force_resume() will be used to resume the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:2069
msgid "Force a device into resume state if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:2071
msgid ""
"This function expects that either pm_runtime_force_suspend() has put the "
"device into a low-power state prior to calling it, or the device had been "
"runtime-suspended before the preceding system-wide suspend transition and it "
"was left in suspend during that transition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:2076
msgid ""
"The actions carried out by pm_runtime_force_suspend(), or by a runtime "
"suspend in general, are reversed and the device is brought back into full "
"power if it is expected to be used on system resume, which is the case when "
"its needs_force_resume flag is set or when its smart_suspend flag is set and "
"its runtime PM status is \"active\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:2082
msgid "In other cases, the resume is deferred to be managed via runtime PM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:322: ../drivers/base/power/runtime.c:2084
msgid "Typically, this function may be invoked from a system resume callback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:103
msgid "Set runtime PM behavior regarding children."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:105
msgid "Whether or not to ignore possible dependencies on children."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:106
msgid ""
"The dependencies of **dev** on its children will not be taken into account "
"by the runtime PM framework going forward if **enable** is ``true``, or they "
"will be taken into account otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:117
msgid "Bump up runtime PM usage counter of a device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:126
msgid "Drop runtime PM usage counter of a device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:128
msgid ""
"Decrement the runtime PM usage counter of **dev** unless it is 0 already."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:137
msgid "Check whether or not a device is runtime-suspended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:139
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:158
msgid ""
"Note that the return value of this function can only be trusted if it is "
"called under the runtime PM lock of **dev** or under conditions in which "
"runtime PM cannot be either disabled or enabled for **dev** and its runtime "
"PM status cannot change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:145
msgid ""
"``true``: **dev** has runtime PM enabled and its status is ``RPM_SUSPENDED``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:146
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:165 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:183
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:200 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:215
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:228 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:255
msgid "``false``: Otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:156
msgid "Check whether or not a device is runtime-active."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:164
msgid ""
"``true``: Runtime PM is disabled for **dev** or its status is ``RPM_ACTIVE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:175
msgid "Check if runtime PM status is \"suspended\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:177
msgid ""
"Note that the return value of this function can only be trusted if it is "
"called under the runtime PM lock of **dev** or under conditions in which the "
"runtime PM status of **dev** cannot change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:182
msgid "``true``: Runtime PM status of **dev** is ``RPM_SUSPENDED``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:192
msgid "Check if runtime PM is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:194
msgid ""
"Note that the return value of this function can only be trusted if it is "
"called under the runtime PM lock of **dev** or under conditions in which "
"runtime PM cannot be either disabled or enabled for **dev**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:199
msgid "``true``: Runtime PM is enabled for **dev**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:209
msgid "Check if runtime PM enabling is blocked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:211
msgid "Do not call this function outside system suspend/resume code paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:214
msgid "``true``: Runtime PM enabling is blocked for **dev**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:224
msgid "Check if runtime PM callbacks may be present."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:227
msgid "``true``: **dev** is marked as having no runtime PM callbacks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:237
msgid "Update the last access time of a device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:239
msgid ""
"Update the last access time of **dev** used by the runtime PM autosuspend "
"mechanism to the current time as returned by ktime_get_mono_fast_ns()."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:249
msgid "Check if runtime PM can work in interrupt context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:252
msgid ""
"``true``: **dev** has been marked as an \"IRQ-safe\" device, in which case "
"its runtime PM callbacks can be expected to work correctly from interrupt "
"handlers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:355
msgid "Conditionally initiate autosuspend of a device or suspend it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:357
msgid ""
"Invoke the \"idle check\" callback of **dev** and, depending on its return "
"value, initiate autosuspend of **dev** or suspend it (depending on whether "
"or not autosuspend has been enabled for it)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:363
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:386 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:413
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:452 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:493
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:599 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:625
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:704 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:736
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:768
msgid "``-EINVAL``: Runtime PM error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:364
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:387 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:414
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:453 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:494
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:600 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:626
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:705 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:737
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:769
msgid "``-EACCES``: Runtime PM disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:365
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:454
msgid ""
"``-EAGAIN``: Runtime PM usage counter non-zero, Runtime PM status change "
"ongoing or device not in ``RPM_ACTIVE`` state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:367
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:390 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:417
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:456 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:497
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:603 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:629
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:708 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:740
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:772
msgid "``-EBUSY``: Runtime PM child_count non-zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:368
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:391 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:418
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:457 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:498
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:604 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:630
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:709 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:741
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:773
msgid "``-EPERM``: Device PM QoS resume latency 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:369
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:458 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:499
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:605 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:631
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:774
msgid "``-EINPROGRESS``: Suspend already in progress."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:370
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:392 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:419
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:459 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:500
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:606 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:632
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:710 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:742
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:775
msgid "``-ENOSYS``: ``CONFIG_PM`` not enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:371
msgid ""
"Other values and conditions for the above values are possible as returned by "
"Runtime PM idle and suspend callbacks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:381
msgid "Suspend a device synchronously."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:384
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:411 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:491
msgid "``1``: Success; device was already suspended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:388
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:415 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:495
msgid ""
"``-EAGAIN``: Runtime PM usage counter non-zero or Runtime PM status change "
"ongoing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:393
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:420 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:711
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:743 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:776
msgid ""
"Other values and conditions for the above values are possible as returned by "
"Runtime PM suspend callbacks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:403
msgid "Update the last access time and initiate autosuspend of a device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:406
msgid ""
"First update the last access time, then initiate autosuspend of **dev** or "
"suspend it (depending on whether or not autosuspend is enabled for it) "
"without engaging its \"idle check\" callback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:431
msgid "Resume a device synchronously."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:434
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:474 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:516
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:538
msgid "``1``: Success; **dev** is already ``RPM_ACTIVE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:445
msgid "Request an asynchronous idle check for a device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:447
msgid ""
"Asynchronously request the PM core to evaluate whether **dev** can be idled "
"or suspended, invoking its ->runtime_idle() callback if provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:468
msgid "Request an asynchronous runtime resume for a device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:470
msgid ""
"Asynchronously request the PM core to resume **dev** to ``RPM_ACTIVE`` state "
"without modifying its usage counter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:485
msgid "Update access time and request delayed suspension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:487
msgid ""
"Update the last access time of **dev** and asynchronously request the PM "
"core to suspend it after the autosuspend delay has elapsed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:510
msgid "Increment usage counter and request asynchronous resume."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:512
msgid ""
"Increment the runtime PM usage counter of **dev** and, if the device is "
"currently suspended, asynchronously request the PM core to resume it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:517
msgid "``0``: Success; runtime-resume was queued."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:527
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:562
msgid "Bump up usage counter of a device and resume it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:529
msgid ""
"Bump up the runtime PM usage counter of **dev** and carry out runtime-resume "
"of it synchronously."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:532
msgid ""
"Note that the runtime PM usage counter of **dev** remains incremented in all "
"cases, even if it returns an error code. Consider using "
"pm_runtime_resume_and_get() instead, especially if the return value is "
"checked by the caller, as this is likely to result in cleaner code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:564
msgid ""
"Resume **dev** synchronously and if that is successful, increment its "
"runtime PM usage counter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:568
msgid ""
"``0``: Success; **dev** is active and its usage counter has been incremented."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:569
msgid "Negative error code on failure; usage counter is unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:578
msgid "Drop device usage counter and request asynchronous idle check."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:580
msgid ""
"Decrement the runtime PM usage counter of **dev**. If the counter reaches "
"zero and the device has no active child dependencies, asynchronously request "
"the PM core to idle or suspend the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:591
msgid "Drop device usage counter and queue autosuspend if 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:593
