"Decrement the runtime PM usage counter of **dev** and if it turns out to be "
"equal to 0, queue up a work item for **dev** like in "
"pm_request_autosuspend()."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:597
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:623 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:702
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:734 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:766
msgid ""
"``1``: Success. Usage counter dropped to zero, but device was already "
"suspended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:601
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:627 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:706
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:738 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:770
msgid ""
"``-EAGAIN``: Runtime PM usage counter became non-zero or Runtime PM status "
"change ongoing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:615
msgid ""
"Update the last access time, drop usage counter and request autosuspend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:618
msgid ""
"Update the last access time of **dev** and decrement its runtime PM usage "
"counter. If the counter drops to zero, asynchronously request the PM core to "
"suspend the device once its autosuspend delay has elapsed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:689
msgid "Drop device usage counter and run \"idle check\" if 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:691
msgid ""
"Decrement the runtime PM usage counter of **dev**. If the counter drops to "
"zero, synchronously evaluate and trigger idle/suspend handling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:694
msgid ""
"Note that this does not update the last access time, but it does respect "
"existing autosuspend timers. If **dev** uses autosuspend, consider using "
"pm_runtime_put_sync_autosuspend() or pm_runtime_put_sync_suspend() instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:698
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:730 ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:762
msgid ""
"The runtime PM usage counter of **dev** remains decremented in all cases, "
"even if it returns an error code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:721
msgid "Drop device usage counter and suspend if 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:723
msgid ""
"Decrement the runtime PM usage counter of **dev**. If the counter drops to "
"zero, suspend the device synchronously."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:726
msgid ""
"This API differs from pm_runtime_put_sync() and "
"pm_runtime_put_sync_autosuspend() in that it ignores any outstanding "
"autosuspend delays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:753
msgid ""
"Update the last access time of a device, drop device usage counter and "
"autosuspend if 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:756
msgid ""
"Update the last access time of **dev** and decrement its runtime PM usage "
"counter. If the counter drops to zero, synchronously suspend the device (or "
"schedule autosuspend if the delay has not elapsed)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:760
msgid ""
"Prefer this API over pm_runtime_put_sync() for devices that use autosuspend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:787
msgid "Set runtime PM status to \"active\" and clear errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:789
msgid ""
"Set the runtime PM status of **dev** to ``RPM_ACTIVE`` and ensure that its "
"dependencies will be taken into account. Also clear the device's error "
"status (**dev->power.runtime_error**)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:793
#: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:816
msgid ""
"It is only valid to call this function if runtime PM is disabled or if **dev-"
">power.runtime_error** is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:796
msgid ""
"This will fail if suppliers cannot be resumed, or if the parent is not in "
"the correct state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:810
msgid "Set runtime PM status to \"suspended\" and clear errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:812
msgid ""
"Set the runtime PM status of **dev** to ``RPM_SUSPENDED`` and ensure that "
"its dependencies will be taken into account. Also clear the device's error "
"status (**dev->power.runtime_error**)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:830
msgid "Disable runtime PM for a device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:832
msgid ""
"Prevent the runtime PM framework from working with **dev** by incrementing "
"its \"disable\" counter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:835
msgid ""
"If the counter is zero when this function runs and there is a pending "
"runtime resume request for **dev**, it will be resumed.  If the counter is "
"still zero at that point, this function cancels all pending runtime PM "
"requests for **dev** and waits for its runtime PM operations to complete (if "
"any)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:840
msgid ""
"For each invocation of this function for **dev**, there must be a matching "
"pm_runtime_enable() call, so that runtime PM is eventually enabled for it "
"again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:851
msgid "Allow autosuspend to be used for a device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:853
msgid ""
"Allow the runtime PM autosuspend mechanism to be used for **dev** whenever "
"requested (or \"autosuspend\" will be handled as direct runtime-suspend for "
"it)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:858
msgid ""
"This is undone automatically with pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend() on "
"driver exit regardless of whether a driver uses managed devm_* functions or "
"not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../power/runtime_pm:325: ../include/linux/pm_runtime.h:868
msgid "Prevent autosuspend from being used."
msgstr ""

